  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-74161",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We factor the cubic by grouping, and simplify until the polynomial is fully factored:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+32x+16 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(2x+1)+16(2x+1) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+16)(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the factor $({x}^{2}+16)$ cannot be factored any further, and it does not have any real roots.\n\nThe only real root of $p(x)$ comes from the factor $(2x+1).$ This factor has a root of $x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and the exponent of the factor is $1.$ Therefore, the root $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$ has multiplicity $1.$\n\nIn conclusion, there is no root with multiplicity $2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
